        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Exeter House\n- People: Earls of Exeter, Charles Edward Stuart\n- Titles: Marquess of Exeter\n- Events: Jacobite Rising of 1745\n- Topics: Peerage of England, Peerage of the United Kingdom\n\nFacts:\n- Exeter House was named for the Earls of Exeter, whose family owned the property until 1757.\n- Charles Edward Stuart stayed at Exeter House during the Jacobite Rising of 1745.\n- Marquess of Exeter is a title that has been created twice, once in the Peerage of England and once in the Peerage of the United Kingdom.",
